01:04:02.710 --> 01:04:05.310
So it's out of distribution.

01:04:05.310 --> 01:04:08.630
And the other comment that I
was making earlier, if you--

01:04:08.630 --> 01:04:11.910
basically, as you increase
the number of documents--

01:04:11.910 --> 01:04:14.495
This particular technique
is able to leverage the fact

01:04:14.495 --> 01:04:16.370
that as you increase
the number of documents,

01:04:16.370 --> 01:04:21.110
you can improve the performance
just because you're not just

01:04:21.110 --> 01:04:22.370
making the context longer.

01:04:22.370 --> 01:04:24.990
You're actually providing
relevant context

01:04:24.990 --> 01:04:26.410
from each of those documents.

01:04:29.077 --> 01:04:30.910
The other big thing
that I want to highlight

01:04:30.910 --> 01:04:32.630
is that in multi-hop
question answering,

01:04:32.630 --> 01:04:35.290
this is particularly relevant
because in multi-hop question

01:04:35.290 --> 01:04:41.930
answering, you do tend to
hit some amount of saturation

01:04:41.930 --> 01:04:44.550
in terms of performance
with standard RAG.

01:04:44.550 --> 01:04:46.970
And even with
Agentic RAG, you do

01:04:46.970 --> 01:04:49.430
tend to hit some
amount of saturation.

01:04:49.430 --> 01:04:52.190
So in HotpotQA,
in 2Wiki, MusiQue,

01:04:52.190 --> 01:04:56.230
or Bamboogle for example, if
you just did RAG, for example,

01:04:56.230 --> 01:04:59.350
you would not hit the
state-of-the-art numbers.

01:04:59.350 --> 01:05:03.190
But with Search-o1, in
a lot of these cases,

01:05:03.190 --> 01:05:05.470
you are hitting the
highest numbers.

01:05:05.470 --> 01:05:09.010
The bolded numbers across
that particular line

01:05:09.010 --> 01:05:12.490
are coming from
Search-o1 as a process.

01:05:12.490 --> 01:05:14.750
So it is providing
a lot of value,

01:05:14.750 --> 01:05:16.490
even in the multi-hop
question answering

01:05:16.490 --> 01:05:18.290
across multiple documents.

01:05:18.290 --> 01:05:18.810
Yes.

01:05:18.810 --> 01:05:22.090
[INAUDIBLE]

01:05:22.090 --> 01:05:26.690
What are the precision and
